## STEP 1 — DELTA

`aygnpacdkgtsfnhgcyjc.supabase.co/*` · supabase gateway (CORS): **CHANGED** — my prior framing ("GoTrue = reflected+ACAC, `/rest/v1/` = wildcard, therefore REST is the safe plane") is **incorrect and now corrected**. Live probes show the split is by *request class, not by plane*: simple (non-preflighted) requests reflect the attacker Origin on **both** planes — `/auth/v1/settings` → `ACAO: https://evil.example` + `ACAC: true`; `/rest/v1/profiles` → `ACAO: https://evil.example`, **no** `ACAC`. The gateway-wide **preflight is uniform**: `OPTIONS /auth/v1/token` (POST+authorization), `OPTIONS /auth/v1/user` (PUT), `OPTIONS /rest/v1/profiles` (GET) all return `ACAO: *`, `ACAH: authorization, apikey, content-type, x-client-info`, `ACAM: GET,HEAD,PUT,PATCH,POST,DELETE,OPTIONS,TRACE,CONNECT`, `max-age: 3600`. Consequence: any origin can issue **header-authenticated** (`Authorization`/`apikey`) cross-origin requests to the whole Supabase project and read the responses — no cookie required. I also noted my last cycle said "first CORS test in 44 days" and framed REST as safe; that understated the data-plane exposure and is corrected here.

