## STEP 5 — NEXT ACTION

```
[NEXT] HUMAN: request two invited test accounts (onecode.de course accounts, distinct emails) from the program
       owner. This single unblock resolves three separate hypotheses at once and is the only thing standing
       between this program and demonstrated impact: (a) the forced-login fragment injection becomes a live PoC;
       (b) the CORS finding's missing input — a real bearer — becomes available, converting the reflected-
       origin channel from "reads auth configuration" to "reads PostgREST table rows" cross-origin; and (c) the
       RLS/BOLA hypothesis (conf 65, open since 2026-09-04) finally gets its two-tenant test design, which is
       now known to be the only non-intrusive path since `external.anonymous_users: false` rules out a free
       second principal. No passive probe can substitute for any of the three.
