**Live delta found — and it falsifies an over-broad claim I made last cycle.**

`/auth/v1/.well-known/` is **not** a uniform reflection surface. It resolves into three distinct classes, and the routing-decisive control (`zzz_ctrl_9x7`) is what makes the split sound rather than sampled:

| Path | Status | ACAO | ACAC | Router |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `/jwks.json`, `/openid-configuration` | 200 | reflected | **true** | GoTrue well-known |
| `/oauth-authorization-server` | 404 `feature_disabled` | **reflected** | **true** | **OAuth server** |
| `/zzz_ctrl_9x7`, `/acme-challenge`, subtree root | 401 | `*` | absent | GoTrue auth gate (fallthrough) |

So the reflection is **route-registered, not subtree-scoped** — and it extends to a *second, disabled* router. My last-cycle line ("the reflection on this subtree is unconditional… any remediation scoped to `/auth/v1/*` resource paths leaves this subtree exposed") was **over-broad and is withdrawn**. `/auth/v1/.well-known/../settings` normalised to `/auth/v1/settings` and was correctly gated at 401 — no traversal bypass.

