[NEW] **The entire pre-gate reflecting surface is unbounded in path space.** All 6 pre-gate route names are prefix-mounted at arbitrary depth: `.well-known/jwks.json/anything`, `.well-known/openid-configuration/anything`, `.well-known/oauth-authorization-server/x`, `.well-known/oauth-authorization-server/wrong-host.example`, `.well-known/oauth-authorization-server/<host>/.well-known/jwks.json`, `oauth/{authorize,token,userinfo}/extra` → all return Kong-local `404 page not found` or `feature_disabled` with reflected `ACAO` + `ACAC: true`, no apikey, arbitrary **and** `Origin: null`, at depth 5 (`a/b/c/d/e`). The RFC 8414 host segment is **not load-bearing** — `wrong-host.example` behaves identically to the real host.
[NEW] **Corrected mechanism — it is not "CORS tiers", it is gate ordering.** `401 {"message":"No API key found in request"}` with `ACAO: *` and no `ACAC` is GoTrue's **global apikey gate, which runs before routing**. Kong's OAuth/OpenID routes are matched **pre-gate**, which is why they reflect credentials without an apikey. Confirmed: `/auth/v1/token` and `/auth/v1/register` — GoTrue's own most important routes — are tier C on both exact and subpath. The observable boundary is therefore *"was a Kong route name matched before the gate?"*, not path shape.
[NEW] Final pre-gate enumeration (8 names tested, credential-free, no apikey): **6 are pre-gate** — `.well-known/jwks.json` (200 ES256), `.well-known/openid-configuration` (200), `.well-known/oauth-authorization-server` (404 `feature_disabled`), `oauth/authorize`, `oauth/token`, `oauth/userinfo` (all 404 `feature_disabled`). **2 are not** — `oauth/register` is pre-gate on exact match only (`register/extra` → 401), and `oauth/oidc` is **not pre-gate at all** (`oidc` and `oidc/extra` both → 401 tier C).
