## Objective
- Continue the OneCode GmbH bug-bounty POC on `aygnpacdkgtsfnhgcyjc.supabase.co`, prioritizing evidence-backed logic flaws and outputting only the required structured analysis blocks.
- Test whether `/auth/v1/verify` exposes a pre-auth token-state/type-validation oracle.

## Important Details
- State: `phase=POC`, `target=api`; report channel `bugs.olivermaicher.eu`.
- Live testing must remain passive-first, `GET`/`HEAD` only, `≤1 rps`, with no customer-data access, auth bypass, or mutation.
- `/auth/v1/verify` is the seventh keyless/pre-gate route, exactly matched and handler-reachable. Off-origin `redirect_to` falls back to `https://kurs.onecode.de`; open redirect is closed.
- OpenID discovery advertises disabled/incorrect capabilities, but only the bounded `/verify` differential is the immediate target.
- Supabase uses ES256 asymmetric JWTs; JWT algorithm confusion and embedded-JWK injection were comprehensively negative.
- Correct publishable-key byte digest: `43ccb834cf7f4cbce3e9e4f8365b819cc36909350ab1e68173c1a47675ea034a`; `870cf518…` includes a trailing newline.
- `GET /storage/v1/bucket → []` is uninformative. The real storage finding is a low-severity `NoSuchBucket` oracle spanning 10 route classes; 81 names were excluded.
- Supabase REST monitor is closed after 27 probes: only `401`/`503`, never `200` or rows.
- `cto.onecode.de` remains `HUMAN_ONLY`: `CNAME cname.perspective-dns.com`, HTTP `409`, no verification TXT.
- Post-auth BOLA remains the highest-value unresolved flaw but requires two invited accounts (`AUTH_HELPED`).

## Work State
### Completed
- Confirmed `/auth/v1/verify` is keyless and credential-reflecting; `/verify/extra` is not mounted.
- Confirmed off-origin `redirect_to` is discarded while on-origin redirects are honored.
- Enumerated `/verify` token parameter forms and several verify types; still need the bounded final type matrix.
- Bounded CORS behavior by route registration: seven pre-gate routes; resource-path reflection occurs only with the public apikey; preflight remains wildcard without `ACAC`.
- Closed JWT confusion, OAuth redirect, SSRF, XSS, forged-cookie, Next.js middleware-bypass, REST exposure, storage public-download, and S3 pre-auth object-access hypotheses.
- Characterized `kurs.onecode.de`: pre-auth `200` set is `{/login,/passwort-vergessen,/datenschutz,/rechtliches}`; protected routes redirect `307→/login`.

### Active
- Highest active lead: `/auth/v1/verify` type-validation separation, confidence `71`, impact `LOW`.
- Secondary finals: route-registration-ordered GoTrue CORS, confidence `69`; bounded storage bucket oracle, confidence `62`.
- Parked: post-auth BOLA `65` (`AUTH_HELPED`), `cto.onecode.de` takeover `58` (`HUMAN_ONLY`), forced-login fragment sink `55` (`AUTH_HELPED`).

### Blocked
- No cheap second authenticated principal: anonymous sign-in and signup are disabled; two invited accounts are required for the BOLA test.
- `cto.onecode.de` cannot progress passively beyond the owner’s claim attempt.
- S3 object authorization requires owner-supplied SigV4 credentials; pre-auth probes only return `403 Missing signature`.

## Next Move
1. Run at `≤1 rps`: `for t in signup invite magiclink recovery email_change email sms phone_change double_factor; do curl -sS -o/dev/null -w "$t %{http_code} " -H "Origin: https://attacker.example" "https://aygnpacdkgtsfnhgcyjc.supabase.co/auth/v1/verify?token=x&type=$t"; done`
2. Compare status, `Location`, `error_code`, and `error_description`; if all invalid-token cases are identical, reduce the oracle to one bit and confidence toward `55`; if type validation precedes token verification, retain/elevate a bounded oracle hypothesis.

