+### CLOSED (NEGATIVE) — /auth/v1/verify token-state oracle — conf 71 -> 20
+
+Ran the queued bounded type matrix (GET only, 1 rps, no tokens supplied, all values synthetic).
+
+**Established validation order: token-presence -> type-validity -> token-lookup.**
+
+1. Token presence is checked first. No token and no token_hash => `400`
+   `{"code":400,"error_code":"validation_failed","msg":"Verify requires a token or a token hash"}`,
+   independent of `type` (confirmed for both `type=signup` and `type=sms`).
+2. `type` is validated next. With any non-empty token, two deterministic response classes:
+   - accepted email-verification types -> `303`, `error_code=otp_expired`,
+     "Email link is invalid or has expired" (164-byte body)
+   - rejected / non-email types -> `303`, `error_code=validation_failed`,
+     "Invalid email verification type" (167-byte body)
+3. Token lookup happens last.
+
+**Type surface (deterministic, stable on re-run, both `Origin: https://attacker.example`
+with `ACAO` reflected + `ACAC: true`):**
+- class A / otp_expired: `signup`, `invite`, `magiclink`, `recovery`, `email_change`, `email`
+- class B / validation_failed: `sms`, `phone_change`, `double_factor`,
+  and also `zzz_bogus`, `idv_`, `enrollment`, `email_otp`, `phone`, `signup_otp`
+
+**Why this does not support the hypothesis.** The original claim was a token-state oracle.
+Tested three structurally different token values (`x`, `aaaaaaaaaa`,
+`00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000`) against `type=recovery`: all three return
+byte-identical `otp_expired`. There is therefore **no observable token-state differential**;
+the generic invalid-token response is constant and non-oracular. `token_hash` (64 zeros)
+with a valid type also returns only the `400` presence error, never reaching lookup.
+
+The residual signal is a **single bit on the `type` parameter** — "is this a recognized
+email-verification type" — and that value set is GoTrue's own static, publicly documented
+list, not a secret. It is additionally gated behind token *presence* (any junk string
+satisfies it), so it yields no state about any token, user, or account.
+
+**Verdict: refuted as an attack primitive.** Informational only, not reportable: no verify
+steps beyond "observe two error strings", no secret disclosed, no auth boundary weakened.
+Confidence 71 -> 20. Do not re-queue.
+
