## Objective
- Act as senior bug bounty analyst for OneCode GmbH (report channel: bugs.olivermaicher.eu), running a 7-step hypothesis cycle over in-scope assets (*.onecode.de, kurs.onecode.de, company infra) to find and validate real, reportable vulnerabilities.
- Output only structured blocks: [PRIO]/[HYP]/[PARKED]/[FINAL]/[NEXT]/[LEARN]/[RISK], passive-first, read-only probes ≤1 rps (GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only).

## Important Details
- Phase: `POC`, target: `api`; risk score currently 49 (deliberately held).
- In-scope only: `*.onecode.de`, `kurs.onecode.de`, OneCode-operated infra. Supabase project `aygnpacdkgtsfnhgcyjc` is treated as in-scope cloud surface.
- Out-of-scope classes list is extensive (enumeration, DoS, TLS/mail best practice, cookie flags, etc.) — never emit those classes.
- Supabase publishable key: `sb_publishable_g48Bd8qEtLesgk0zgzTRig_eZ6j9w30`; sha256 of key bytes = `43ccb834cf7f4cbce3e9e4f8365b819cc36909350ab1e68173c1a47675ea034a` (the `870cf518…` digest was a trailing-newline artifact; PoCs must cite `43ccb834…`).
- `kurs.onecode.de` build fingerprints: main chunk `0-mbmp1iqb6hj.js` = 154 581 B sha256 `f916f314ea61a8c58a055707fc63c251f38e8412ae7a08e6abd7500ec375abca`; sink chunk `1a4tqdnsy9k1l.js` = 13 880 B sha256 `5a72d2cd8738ecadfd9ef271f062b3f2ba799617dabddf32987c2883c6dcedd0` (64-hex, never the 66-char variant); `/login` page sha256 `99798c7d94a15abf93ec349b0b221a89dfba756cb21fc581a09d37acd21d9450`, 18 702 B. No deploy since 2026-09-19 11:33Z; build-diffing is event-triggered only.
- Pre-auth surface on kurs = `{/login, /passwort-vergessen, /datenschutz, /rechtliches}` (200); all `/api/*, /v1, /admin, /dashboard, /courses, /einladung, /passwort-neu` → 307→/login.
- `HashSessionHandoff` (module 34891) mounted on `/login` RSC payload row 18, no state/nonce/PKCE binding; post-setSession map `{invite:/einladung, recovery:/passwort-neu}` default `/` — forced-login (CWE-384) only, requires valid attacker token pair → PARKED (AUTH_HELPED).
- GoTrue CORS model: three tiers keyed on route registration — (A) 6 pre-gate Kong routes (`.well-known/jwks.json`, `.well-known/openid-configuration`, `.well-known/oauth-authorization-server` prefix-mounted, `oauth/authorize`, `oauth/token`, `oauth/userinfo`) reflect Origin+ACAC:true keyless; (B) `/auth/v1/*` resource paths reflect+ACAC only when apikey present (header or query), else `ACAO: *` no ACAC; (C) fallthrough → `ACAO: *` + 9-method list + max-age 3600. `/auth/v1/verify` is the 7th pre-gate route (keyless, exactly-matched). Preflight NEVER reflects anywhere. Mechanism = gate ordering (GoTrue apikey gate before routing; Kong routes matched pre-gate).
- JWT signing is **ES256-only** (JWKS kid `4f59d46f-c3e6-47c7-a717-fabf016650c9`); 38 live probes closed alg confusion + embedded JWK injection; old HS256-secret reasoning was wrong-algorithm.
- `/auth/v1/settings`: `external.anonymous_users:false`, `disable_signup:true`, `mailer_autoconfirm:false`, email-only, `saml_enabled:false` but `saml_private_key_next_configured:true`, `passkeys_enabled:false`. No allowlist enumeration in settings body.
- `redirect_to` allowlist: 15 off-origin shapes across 4 verify types + 2 token encodings, zero bypass; `X-Forwarded-Host` does not influence it; SITE_URL = `https://kurs.onecode.de`.
- Storage: pre-auth bucket-existence oracle route-table-complete across 10 mounted GET classes (byte-identical `400 {"code":"NoSuchBucket"}`), 81 names excluded, bucket name unrecoverable from 13 pre-auth chunks; `/object/upload/sign/{b}/{k}` mounted (POST outside read-only bounds). S3 plane (`aygnpacdkgtsfnhgcyjc.storage.supabase.co/storage/v1/s3`) = SigV4-enforced, 403 Missing signature, no oracle, untestable without owner keys → PARKED (was wrongly emitted `[FINAL] conf 75 PASSIVE HIGH` with empty verify_steps).
- `cto.onecode.de`: CNAME→`cname.perspective-dns.com` (104.18.2.73/104.18.3.73), HTTP 409 "error code:1001", zero verification TXT, day-58+ → conf 58, HUMAN_ONLY.
- REST monitor `/rest/v1/` formally closed 09-17 (27 probes 503↔401, never 200+rows).
- Methodological rule: any scope claim must carry its own negative control (counter-example path); re-derive every hash live with 64-hex assertion before recording.
- Ranked lead from another agent: `[75] aygnpacdkgtsfnhgcyjc.storage.supabase.co/storage/v1/s3` (already downgraded by self-correction to PARKED/untestable).

## Work State
### Completed
- 53+ days of cycles; pre-auth surface of kurs fully characterized and exhausted.
- Closed/rejected: XSS on `/login` (enum + server allowlist), `_next/image` SSRF, CVE-2025-29927 middleware bypass, path-normalization/header-desync bypasses, forged-cookie bypasses, PKCE injection, open redirect (GoTrue 15 shapes + HashSessionHandoff next-map), JWT alg/key confusion + embedded JWK (38 probes), HS256 secret forgery, storage bucket-name recovery, SSO assertion injection, host-header redirect influence, CORS cache amplification, `/auth/v1/anonymous`, PostgREST schema/GraphQL disclosure, analytics plane.
- Established [FINAL] conf ≥40 PASSIVE findings: (1) pre-auth token-state oracle on `/auth/v1/verify` conf 71; (2) route-registration-ordered CORS/auth gate conf 69 (LOW-MEDIUM); (3) storage bucket-existence oracle conf 62 (LOW).

### Active
- Queued NEXT probe (from last lead): enumerate verification-type surface on `/auth/v1/verify` — read-only GETs with `token=x` and types `{signup,invite,magiclink,recovery,email_change,email,sms,phone_change,double_factor}` plus Origin header, to test whether parameter validation is separable from token lookup (distinct error_code per type before token verification).
- New standing hypotheses: CORS reflection on `/verify` unconditional across both response branches; verification-type enumeration disclosing configured OTP channels.

### Blocked
- Post-auth BOLA/RLS (conf 65): needs 2 invited test accounts → AUTH_HELPED.
- `cto.onecode.de` takeover (conf 58): needs owner claim attempt → HUMAN_ONLY.
- S3 plane differential: needs owner-supplied SigV4 keys → PARKED.
- HashSessionHandoff forced-login: needs valid token pair + victim interaction → AUTH_HELPED.

