**[DELTA #1 — queued probe executed] `GET /auth/v1/user`, apikey + evil Origin**
- With `apikey` present: `401 no_authorization`, `ACAO: https://evil.example` + `ACAC: true`, `vary: Origin` → **Tier B confirmed unchanged** on authenticated resource paths (Origin reflected + credentials allowed once apikey gate passes).
- Control without Origin → no ACAO header at all.
- Preflight `OPTIONS` (authorization,apikey requested): `ACAO: *` + 9-method list, **no ACAC, never reflects** → preflight ceiling confirmed.
- **Bounding consequence:** any *credentialed* cross-origin read is browser-blocked (preflight `ACAO: *` w/o ACAC is invalid for `credentials:include`). Only `credentials:omit` reads succeed, and those carry no cookies (GoTrue auth = Bearer header, no session cookie; the only `supabase.co` cookie is `__cf_bm` bot-mgmt). Exploit payload = evil-JS reading data it already holds the JWT to call directly. **Impact drops; [69] CORS finding recount to conf ~55, LOW.**

**[DELTA #2 — queued probe executed] `/auth/v1/verify` type-surface enumeration (9 types, ≤1 rps)**
- `signup|invite|magiclink|recovery|email_change|email` → all **identical** `303 otp_expired`; no per-type differential.
- `sms|phone_change|double_factor` → `303 validation_failed "Invalid email verification type"` (clean separation: email-verify typed vs not).
- `redirect_to=https://evil.example/steal` **ignored in all shapes** → Location always `kurs.onecode.de` → open-redirect re-closed (15+ shapes now).
- Token-state oracle: missing/empty token → `400 "Verify requires a token or a token hash"`; any present invalid token (64-hex garbage *or* well-formed but forged ES256 JWT) → `303 otp_expired`. **No valid-token differential observable pre-auth, no identity/state leakage in any branch.**
- All 303/400s reflect Origin + ACAC (harmless — no sensitive data in fragments/bodies).

**[FINAL]**
- **[71] verify token-state oracle: DEAD.** Residual signal = token present/absent (title-case parameter validation, rejected class).
- **[69] CORS gate-ordering: SURVIVED but downgraded** → reflect+ACAC confirmed on authenticated paths; browser exploitability bounded by preflight `ACAO:*`/no-ACAC ceiling → conf ~55, LOW.
- Ranking now: [75] S3 plane (PARKED/AUTH_HELPED), PARKED BOLA conf 65 (AUTH_HELPED, 2 accounts), cto conf 58 (HUMAN_ONLY), CORS ~55. **Pre-auth surface of kurs.onecode.de/Supabase is now exhaustively closed** — every remaining positive hypothesis is AUTH_HELPED or HUMAN_ONLY.

**[NEXT]**
1. `curl …GET /auth/v1/verify?type=signup` with a **real** signup link (from an invited-profile email) to test valid-token behaviour — AUTH_HELPED.
2. BOLA/RLS differential on `/auth/v1/users` (and PostgREST) with two invited accounts — AUTH_HELPED.
3. `cto.onecode.de` owner-claim — HUMAN_ONLY.

**[LEARN]** The preflight `ACAO:*`/no-ACAC invariant is what actually neutralizes nearly all reflected-origin+ACAC findings on GoTrue; the 6-vs-3 type split shows GoTrue validates against an email-Verify-only type set server-side, and `redirect_to` is only consulted for a *successful* token (not probeable pre-auth).

**[RISK]** Program risk ~49–70 (unchanged; no new findings emitted this cycle).

**[STOP → REQUEST]** All further progress requires the two invited test accounts (BOLA/RLS, S3, valid-token verify). No additional pre-auth probes are queued — further cycling on this surface has ~zero marginal value. Confirm accounts or redirect to a different scope item.
