## DELTA
- **Verify type surface CLOSED**: `/auth/v1/verify` accepts email types `{signup, invite, magiclink, recovery, email_change, email}` (303→Site URL, `otp_expired`); rejects phone types `{sms, phone_change, double_factor}` (303, `validation_failed` "Invalid email verification type"). Off-origin `redirect_to=https://evil.example/steal` discarded → Site URL fallback. Confirms email-only backend + per-type allowlist; no cross-type confusion, no open redirect.
- **CORS reflection re-confirmed on pre-gate routes**: simple GET with `Origin: https://evil.example` on `/auth/v1/user` (401) and `/auth/v1/token` (405) returns `access-control-allow-origin: https://evil.example` + `access-control-allow-credentials: true` + `vary: Origin`. Preflight OPTIONS returns `ACAO: *` with no `ACAC`. Impact stays **LOW** (bearer-token auth; no ambient cookies on `supabase.co`).
- **No net-new surface**: crt.sh down (502); hackertarget returns only the 5 known hosts; DNS brute of 15 candidate labels = all NXDOMAIN. Host set unchanged (`onecode.de`, `kurs`, `cto`, `www`, `mail`, `mta-sts`).
- **Storage/REST unchanged**: S3 no-sig 403; REST monitor root 401. No state change vs. prior cycle.

## PRIORITIZE
1. `[PARKED]` Post-auth BOLA via Supabase RLS gap (conf 65, AUTH_HELPED) — only HIGH-value path; blocked on lab accounts.
2. `[FINAL]` Reflected-origin credentialed CORS on GoTrue (conf 85) — real but bounded LOW; reportable as INFO/LOW hardening.
3. `[FINAL]` S3-plane independent SigV4 authz (conf 75) — HIGH ceiling but untestable without owner keys.
4. `[PARKED]` cto.onecode.de takeover (conf 58, HUMAN_ONLY) — claim attempt only.
5. `[FINAL]` Token-state oracle / CORS route-gate / storage bucket oracle (conf 62–71) — LOW informational.

## HYPOTHESES
- `[FINAL]` GoTrue gate reflects arbitrary Origin with credentials on pre-gate routes; no cookie-auth path → LOW.
- `[FINAL]` S3 storage plane enforces independent SigV4 that bypasses PostgREST RLS → HIGH ceiling, unverified.
- `[PARKED]` RLS gap enables cross-tenant BOLA once any two authenticated sessions exist.
- `[PARKED]` Perspective dangling CNAME on `cto.onecode.de` is claimable.
- `[REFUTED]` `verify` open-redirect / type-confusion.
- `[REFUTED]` JWT alg-confusion, `/auth/v1/verify` redirect, x-middleware-subrequest, path-norm/header desync.

## SELF-CRITIQUE
- This cycle was pure re-measurement + failed OSINT (crt.sh 502); zero new attack surface. Continuing passive probes has severely diminishing returns.
- CORS: tempting to inflate, but without a cookie-based session the reflected-ACAO+ACAC is not exploitable — must not misreport as token theft.
- S3-plane #3 cannot be validated from environment; asserting exploitability would be speculation, not measurement.
- Every remaining HIGH path requires an authorization artifact (invited account) or owner action — this is a coverage gap, not a vuln.

