[PHASE] POC | target: api | 2026-10-07 | mode: read-only GET/HEAD/OPTIONS, ≤1 rps
[PRIO]  HIGH — queued [NEXT] (type-surface enum on /verify) executed; produced a hard contradiction
        against an existing [FINAL]. Correction beats new leads: the pre-gate route inventory was
        incomplete and one mechanism claim ("verify is exactly-matched") is now falsified by
        /auth/v1/verify/a/b/c/d → 404 + keyless reflection + ACAC=true. Next spend goes to closing
        the corrected route table, not to time-cadence re-probes.
[HYP]   H1: /auth/v1/verify `type` enumerates configured OTP channels (PARKED, conf 30).
        H2: /auth/v1/authorize `provider` differentiates configured vs unknown providers.
        H3: pre-gate (tier A) route set is exactly 7, with /auth/v1/verify exactly-matched.
[FINAL]
  F1 — [FINAL] CORRECTION: route-registration-ordered CORS (prior conf 69) → conf 74, impact unchanged.
        Observed pre-gate / keyless-reflecting prefixes on api host = 10, not 7:
        .well-known/{jwks.json,openid-configuration,oauth-authorization-server}, oauth/{authorize,token,userinfo},
        /auth/v1/verify*   (PREFIX, depth-unbounded: /verify/ →400, /verify/a/b/c/d →404, all ACAC=true)
        /auth/v1/callback* (NEW, 8th; 303 → Site URL always)
        /auth/v1/sso/saml/acs* /auth/v1/sso/saml/metadata* (NEW; 404 + ACAC=true)
        Mechanism survives, inventory was wrong: /auth/v1/logout|user|factors|token|settings|health|
        signup|otp|magiclink|invite|recover|resend|admin/*|phone/*|sso/authorize|sso/oidc/authorize
        → 401 + fallthrough `ACAO: *` (unconditional, also with no Origin) = tier C/B, not tier A.
        Blast radius bounded: storage host returns 404 + zero CORS headers on all 5 same paths
        (per-host gateway, no cross-host inheritance).
        verify_steps: for each path above, `curl -D- -H 'Origin: https://evil.example'` and record
        HTTP code + ACAO + ACAC + Location; repeat with Origin omitted to prove conditionality.
  F2 — [FINAL] token-state oracle conf 71 → 76 (controls now complete):
        400 validation_failed = param absent/empty (no token / token= / no type);
        303 otp_expired = token present + type in {signup,invite,magiclink,recovery,email_change,email};
        303 validation_failed "Invalid email verification type" = type in {sms,phone_change,double_factor};
        off-origin redirect_to and %0a Set-Cookie injection both collapse to
        `https://kurs.onecode.de#...` — allowlist + fragment fallback hold on the redirecting path.
  F3 — [REJECTED] H1: type param is validated against the *email-verification type set* (endpoint
        scope), not against configured channels → no OTP-channel disclosure. Not a latent finding.
  F4 — [REJECTED] H2: /authorize discriminates "provider is not enabled" (registry-known: 20/20 of
        azure,apple,bitbucket,discord,facebook,figma,github,gitlab,google,keycloak,kakao,notion,
        slack,spotify,twitch,twitter,zoom) vs "Provider X could not be found" (web3,linear,ethereum,
