- 2026-10-03 ACCEPTED MISCONFIG @ aygnpacdkgtsfnhgcyjc.supabase.co/auth/v1: **preflight does not reflect anywhere, on any tier.** `OPTIONS` on `/auth/v1/oauth/authorize`, `/auth/v1/oauth/token`, `/auth/v1/.well-known/jwks.json` and the fallthrough control all return `200 ACAO: *` + the 9-method list + `max-age 3600` with **no `ACAC`**. Therefore the credentialed reflection is reachable only as a *simple* request — i.e. via the `?apikey=` query-string channel, which needs no preflight and no attacker-set header. This narrows the browser-exploitability of the finding to a single, already-catalogued mechanism instead of leaving it open-ended.
