**DELTA**
- Probed `/auth/v1/verify?type=recovery&token=<64hex>` (bare, + on-origin `redirect_to`, + non-hex XSS payload, + invalid `type`, + fragment-bearing `redirect_to`): all 303 to `https://kurs.onecode.de[on-origin-path]#error=access_denied&error_code=otp_expired&error_description=Email+link+is+invalid+or+has+expired&sb=`. Fragment fields are server-controlled enums only; `sb=` empty; token/type not reflected; attacker fragment in `redirect_to` stripped and replaced by server fragment.
- On-origin `redirect_to=https://kurs.onecode.de/ok?x=MARKER42` preserved verbatim → query survives, but that is allowlist-intended behavior (path+query on app origin).
- `redirect_to=https://kurs.onecode.de/login?next=https://evil.example/` passes allowlist (host on-origin). Followed: `/login?next=<evil>` returns 200 and echoes `next` only in the RSC flight URL (`"q":"?next=..."`); no client chunk reads `searchParams.get("next")` (grep over main `0-mbmp1iqb6hj.js`, sink `1a4tqdnsy9k1l.js`, and all 6 other login chunks — only hit is Next's internal `NEXT_RSC_UNION_QUERY`).
- LoginForm success path hardcodes `c.push("/")` — `next` not consumed post-auth. HashSessionHandoff: `next = {invite,recovery}[type] ?? "/"` fixed map, `setSession()` server-validated, error path fixed `/login?error=...`.
- Re-derived chunk hashes live: main `f916f314ea61a8c58a055707fc63c251f38e8412ae7a08e6abd7500ec375abca` (154581 B), sink `5a72d2cd8738ecadfd9ef271f062b3f2ba799617dabddf32987c2883c6dcedd0` (13880 B) — both match baseline, no deploy since 2026-09-19.
- Delta: **NO_DELTA**. Surface unchanged; two candidate chains falsified (verify→fragment injection; verify→`next`→open redirect).

**PRIORITIZE**
1. HUMAN/AUTH_HELPED — BOLA via RLS gap (conf 65), needs 2 invited accounts: sole path to CRITICAL.
2. HUMAN_ONLY — cto.onecode.de Perspective claim (conf 58, day-59+).
3. PASSIVE/HUMAN_ONLY — S3 SigV4 plane `aygnpacdkgtsfnhgcyjc.storage.supabase.co/storage/v1/s3` (owner keys required).
4. Parked — storage bucket-name oracle (route-table-complete, 81 names excluded, pre-auth unrecoverable).

**HYPOTHESES**
- H1 (falsified this cycle): verify 303 fragment reflects attacker input → app-origin fragment injection into HashSessionHandoff parser. Disproved: all fragment values server-set enums, `sb=` empty, token/type unreflected, `redirect_to` fragment stripped.
- H2 (falsified this cycle): `/login?next=<off-origin>` is a post-auth open redirect reachable via verify `redirect_to`. Disproved: `next` echoed only in RSC flight URL; zero consumers across all 7 login chunks; LoginForm hardcodes `push("/")`; HashSessionHandoff `next` is a fixed map, not the query param.
- H3 (held, AUTH_HELPED): `/rest/v1/{profiles,enrollments}` cross-tenant read under RLS gap — unverifiable without 2 invited accounts.
- H4 (held, HUMAN_ONLY): cto.onecode.de registration claim via Perspective DNS.

**SELF-CRITIQUE**
- Both falsifications rest on static analysis of all 7 chunks referenced by `/login` + live hash verification — grep coverage is complete for this build; residual risk only if server components consume `searchParams` invisibly (server login page has no redirect on GET — probe showed 200 render, no 3xx — so no server-side redirect either).
- `sb=` empty on error path is unobserved on the success path (requires valid token, out of passive bounds) — bounded, not claimed closed.

**NEXT**
[NEXT] HUMAN — request two invited `kurs.onecode.de` test accounts, password-grant, cross-query `GET /rest/v1/profiles?select=id,email,tenant_id` and `/rest/v1/enrollments` with account A's Bearer to confirm the RLS gap (config 65, priority-1). Fallback if accounts denied: Perspective claim attempt on cto.onecode.de (HUMAN_ONLY, conf 58). No further passive probes productive — surface converged; re-probe cadence ≤1/day, build-diff event-triggered only.

**LEARN**
- GoTrue `verify` composes app-origin 303 fragments exclusively from server-side enums (`error_code`/`error_description`); attacker inputs (`token`, `type`, `redirect_to` fragment) never enter the fragment — the app-origin redirect is not an injection primitive.
- kurs `/login?next=` is a dead parameter in this build: echoed in flight data, never read, never used by LoginForm — do not re-test open-redirect via `next` unless a deploy changes the chunk hashes.
- Each claim carries its own negative control: chunk-hash re-derivation (both 64-hex, match baseline) + per-chunk grep for `searchParams.get("next")` (zero hits, control = `NEXT_RSC_UNION_QUERY` present).

**RISK**
Risk score: **49 (steady)**. No demonstrated customer data access pre-auth; passives converged; top-3 leads all gated on HUMAN/AUTH_HELPED action.
