# 7-Question Gate Triage

## Lead 1: Railway App API Discovery (bigpickle, confidence 40)
| Q | Question | Answer | Reason |
|---|----------|--------|--------|
| Q1 | In scope? | YES | kurs.onecode.de matches *.onecode.de |
| Q2 | Attacker reachable? | YES | Public HTTP endpoints |
| Q3 | Real security impact? | NO | API discovery is reconnaissance, not a vulnerability |
| Q4 | Provable non-invasively? | YES | Simple HEAD/GET requests |
| Q5 | Novel? | NO | Standard recon step, not a finding |
| Q6 | Not on always-rejected list? | YES | Not explicitly rejected |
| Q7 | Would a reasonable triager accept? | NO | No evidence of actual vulnerability |

**Verdict: INVALID** — Reconnaissance only; no security impact without evidence of exposed endpoints, auth bypass, or data exposure.

---

## Lead 2: Session Fixation on kurs.onecode.de (bigpickle/nemotron3, confidence 65)
| Q | Question | Answer | Reason |
|---|----------|--------|--------|
| Q1 | In scope? | YES | kurs.onecode.de is in-scope asset |
| Q2 | Attacker reachable? | YES | Public login page |
| Q3 | Real security impact? | YES | Session fixation → account takeover |
| Q4 | Provable non-invasively? | PARTIAL | Requires test account + authenticated session comparison |
| Q5 | Novel? | MAYBE | Railway default session handling needs verification |
| Q6 | Not on always-rejected list? | YES | Session fixation is not rejected |
| Q7 | Would a reasonable triager accept? | YES | If session ID not regenerated post-login |

**Verdict: HOLD** — Needs live verification: (1) GET /login, capture Set-Cookie; (2) POST login with test creds, verify session ID changes; (3) check Secure/HttpOnly/SameSite flags. Cannot confirm without authenticated probe.

---

