## Important Details
- In-scope only: `*.onecode.de`, `kurs.onecode.de`, and company-owned infra reachable from those (Supabase project + storage host are in-scope as app backend).
- Passive-first rules: GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only, ≤1 rps; no mutating tests, no auth-bypass attempts against live customer data; no credentialed attacks; no username enumeration / brute-force / rate-limit classes (out of scope).
- Phase: `POC`, target: `api`.
- Publishable key: `sb_publishable_g48Bd8qEtLesgk0zgzTRig_eZ6j9w30` (sha256 of key bytes = `43ccb834cf7f4cbce3e9e4f8365b819cc36909350ab1e68173c1a47675ea034a`; the older `870cf518…` digest was a trailing-newline artifact — all PoCs must cite `43ccb834…`).
